# Changelog

## Unreleased

- Fixed every default `subagent` spawn failing on pi 0.85.1: the extension passed a `--session-control` flag that pi does not implement, so children exited immediately with `Unknown option: --session-control`. Session control now hands each child a deterministic `--session <path>` file under `~/.pi/agent/sessions/collaborating-agents-subagents/`, which also makes process-mode transcripts tailable from launch instead of waiting for child registration or fallback discovery. `sessionControl: false` still opts out and keeps the previous discovery behavior.
- Fixed subagent type `model` pins bypassing availability validation. Pins are now checked against the model registry before spawn and degrade to the session model with a warning (this also catches case mismatches such as `GPT-5.3-codex-spark`). Because registry presence does not prove account entitlement, a pin that is rejected at request time (for example `Codex error: The 'gpt-5.4-mini' model is not supported when using Codex with a ChatGPT account.`) now triggers one retry with the session model, and model warnings are surfaced in the completion message body rather than only in tool `details`.
- Retain recorded V3 subtasks after completion, reopening and task selection. Ordinary child progress automatically completes the parent after the last child, and reopening a child reopens the parent; governed finalize checks the accepted task and its retained children after verification/review.

- Default Task Plan to readable `pi-plan/v3`: current requirements, current-only rolling detail, concise edits and ordinary manual completion without runtime state.
- Preserve V1/V2 through explicit `legacy-index.ts` selection and read-only views; migration remains preview-only. Named legacy APIs moved to that entry, and legacy configuration through the default entry is awaitable.
- Add an optional governed host with bound Human confirmation, real scoped execution, verification/review/finalize, cancellation and inspected recovery behind the readable Plan.

- Added `/control:enter` as the required one-action handoff after Agent-tool initialization, using the remembered control path so the command stays short and the Human-in-the-Loop workflow continues from the control repository.
- Added name-only Agent initialization: a local creation request with a workspace name now derives `<cwd>/<name>_control` and `<cwd>/<name>_code` without asking the user to supply redundant absolute paths.
- Added a name-first `/control:init` path that creates `<name>_control` and `<name>_code` together, plus a separate existing-repositories path with immediate validation, visible profile defaults, and an explicit final apply action.
- Fixed post-initialization commands to keep using the newly created control repository for the current Pi session; missing-index status now asks for an initialized control path instead of incorrectly requesting initialization again.
- Added safe post-init Pi navigation: interactive initialization continues the persisted conversation in a new session rooted at the control repository, while non-persisted sessions receive an exact restart command.
- Added a template-first control workspace extension with four Agent tools, five Human-UI commands, versioned repository bindings, managed `AGENTS.md` rules, deterministic doctor checks, and explicitly authorized local Git bootstrap.
- Hardened control workspace remote redaction, rebind identity checks, revisable Human previews and preview identity, cross-process stale-write rejection and exclusive transaction locking, persisted path boundaries, canonical AGENTS verification, preview result semantics, and new-file rollback.
- Clarified generated Git governance so plans and plugins are split into reviewable delivery-slice PRs instead of being treated as one oversized feature PR.
- Added a human-gated `spec.md` → `plan.md` → `tasks.md` planning extension with deterministic validation and task convergence.
- Fixed subagent launch tool filtering so extension tools such as `agent_message` remain active in spawned agents.
- Fixed Pi 0.65+ compatibility by relying on `session_start` for session replacement lifecycle events instead of the removed `session_switch` and `session_fork` hooks.
